{"type":"message","id":"677eada9","parentId":"936ddd02","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:36:05.324Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-02-18 19:06 GMT+5:30] URGENT: End-to-end automated fix for the 5-10 second gateway restart flicker. Steps: 1) Use OpenClaw exec tool (host=gateway) to run: `schtasks /query /fo LIST /v` and filter for any task that runs `openclaw`, `gateway`, or `node`. 2) Also exec `sc query state= all` and look for a service named OpenClawGateway or similar. 3) Check for any running `cmd.exe` processes with command lines containing `openclaw-wrapper` or `gateway`. 4) If a repeating scheduled task is found, output the exact `schtasks /delete /tn \"TaskName\" /f` command to disable it. 5) If a service is misconfigured, output the `sc stop` and `sc delete` commands. 6) If a startup batch file is found, output the `del` command. 7) Return only the precise command(s) to execute to stop the loop. Do not ask for user input."}],"timestamp":1771421765319}}
